{
 "thread": "bMKJRWu1v6Y",
 "subject": "How Can I generate all structure output files and images as generated in window structure software? Please can you share this script here with your given example data set",
 "messages_listed": 2,
 "last_activity": "2024-11-05T04:14:12Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "rd8OgiuMAAAJ",
   "from": "Rajneesh Paliwal",
   "author": "bc6aaaa25ff9a3a0",
   "date": "2024-10-31T10:49:47Z",
   "subject": "How Can I generate all structure output files and images as generated in window structure software? Please can you share this script here with your given example data set",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"font-size:16px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Aptos;margin:0px 10px\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Dear Luis,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">I have recently seen you added structure analysis using the greenlight object option in dartR.  Thanks for adding it in dartR.</span><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><br></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">Using the window structure software, all analysis results are saved in the default directory. How can I do the same here to save all my files in the default directory after completing all analyses?<span> How can I  add my population name later and generate structure bar plot for particular cluster/group of K4 (when Delta K results are very precise)   and also other K3 to K5 where DeltK results are not precise and show structure between K3-K5. </span></span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><br></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"> How can I give its color automatically for 12 population groups rather than the code you gave above?</span></span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span><br></span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><br></span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">You can add above request scripts in following your given example for structure. It will be helpful for many other to use it as user friendly.</span></span></span></p></div></div></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"font-size:16px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Aptos;margin:0px 10px\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">out_struc &lt;-<span> </span>gl.run.structure(gl5[,1:100], k.range=2:5, num.k.rep=10, exec=&quot;./structure/structure&quot;, noadmix=FALSE)</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">out_evanno &lt;- gl.evanno(out_struc, plot.out=TRUE) #check deltaK for correct estimation of number of clusters (Evanno et al., 2005)</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">qmat &lt;- gl.plot.structure(out_struc, colors_clusters=c(&quot;#A6CEE3&quot;, &quot;#1F78B4&quot;, &quot;#33A02C&quot;), K=3)</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">gl.map.structure(qmat, gl5[,1:100], K=3)</span></p></div></div></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"font-size:16px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Aptos;margin:0px 10px\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><br></span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Thanks for your help.</span></span></span></p></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"verdana, sans-serif\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:medium;margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"color:black;font-size:10pt\">Rajneesh Paliwal, PhD (DAAD\r\nFellow)</span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\">Associate Scientist</span><br></p><p style=\"font-size:medium;margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;text-align:justify;font-size:12.8px\">Genetic Resources Center</span></p><p style=\"font-size:medium;margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;text-align:justify;font-size:12.8px\">International Inst. for Tropical\r\nAgriculture</span></p><p style=\"font-size:medium;margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;text-align:justify;font-size:12.8px\">Oyo Road PMB-5320, Ibadan, Nigeria</span></p></font></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
