  {
   "id": "Hc40R_X9BwAJ",
   "from": "Jose Luis Mijangos",
   "author": "592079bda2cb3220",
   "date": "2024-11-05T04:14:12Z",
   "subject": "Re: How Can I generate all structure output files and images as generated in window structure software? Please can you share this script here with your given example data set",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Rajneesh,<div><br></div><div>I have updated the function so the outflies are not deleted (see code below). To use this updated function, please install the developing version of dartR.popgen as shown in the code below.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Luis </div><div><br></div><div>#installing developing version<br>devtools::install_github(&quot;green-striped-gecko/dartR.popgen@dev&quot;)<br>library(dartRverse)<br>t1 &lt;- <a href=\"http://platypus.gl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://platypus.gl&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457656610000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0PM6Sx9gKl0-8BSqI1N5Ws\">platypus.gl</a><br>t1 &lt;- gl.filter.callrate(t1,threshold = 1,mono.rm = T)<br># set delete.files to FALSE<br>res &lt;- gl.run.structure(t1,<br>                        k.range = 2:4,<br>                        delete.files = F)<br># pop labels are shown at the top of the plot<br># plot only for k = 4<br>gl.plot.structure(res,<br>                  K = 4)<br># plot a range of K, 2 to 4<br>gl.plot.structure(res,<br>                  K = 2:4)<br># colors for bar plot<br>bar_col &lt;- c(&quot;yellow&quot;,&quot;red&quot;,&quot;green&quot;,&quot;blue&quot;)<br>gl.plot.structure(res,<br>                  K = 2:4,<br>                  color_clusters = bar_col)<br><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thursday 31 October 2024 at 9:49:47 pm UTC+11 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rajnees...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"font-size:16px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Aptos;margin:0px 10px\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Dear Luis,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">I have recently seen you added structure analysis using the greenlight object option in dartR.  Thanks for adding it in dartR.</span><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><br></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">Using the window structure software, all analysis results are saved in the default directory. How can I do the same here to save all my files in the default directory after completing all analyses?<span> How can I  add my population name later and generate structure bar plot for particular cluster/group of K4 (when Delta K results are very precise)   and also other K3 to K5 where DeltK results are not precise and show structure between K3-K5. </span></span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><br></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"> How can I give its color automatically for 12 population groups rather than the code you gave above?</span></span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span><br></span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><br></span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">You can add above request scripts in following your given example for structure. It will be helpful for many other to use it as user friendly.</span></span></span></p></div></div></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"font-size:16px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Aptos;margin:0px 10px\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">out_struc &lt;-<span> </span>gl.run.structure(gl5[,1:100], k.range=2:5, num.k.rep=10, exec=&quot;./structure/structure&quot;, noadmix=FALSE)</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">out_evanno &lt;- gl.evanno(out_struc, plot.out=TRUE) #check deltaK for correct estimation of number of clusters (Evanno et al., 2005)</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">qmat &lt;- gl.plot.structure(out_struc, colors_clusters=c(&quot;#A6CEE3&quot;, &quot;#1F78B4&quot;, &quot;#33A02C&quot;), K=3)</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">gl.map.structure(qmat, gl5[,1:100], K=3)</span></p></div></div></blockquote><blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"font-size:16px;color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Aptos;margin:0px 10px\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><br></span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:14px;font-size:10pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:15.4px;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Thanks for your help.</span></span></span></p></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"verdana, sans-serif\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:medium;margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"color:black;font-size:10pt\">Rajneesh Paliwal, PhD (DAAD\r\nFellow)</span><span style=\"color:black\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\">Associate Scientist</span><br></p><p style=\"font-size:medium;margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;text-align:justify;font-size:12.8px\">Genetic Resources Center</span></p><p style=\"font-size:medium;margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;text-align:justify;font-size:12.8px\">International Inst. for Tropical\r\nAgriculture</span></p><p style=\"font-size:medium;margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;text-align:justify;font-size:12.8px\">Oyo Road PMB-5320, Ibadan, Nigeria</span></p></font></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n</blockquote></div>"
